EctoPad Aurora renderer compatibility experiment (REJECTED), 2026-08-13

The physical iPad screenshot at 12:04 shows large black and incorrectly
translucent world polygons, while HUD and some room surfaces remain correct.
This is renderer/material-state corruption, not a brightness adjustment.

EctoPad remains pinned to Aurora 5143394. Four later official Aurora fixes
apply cleanly without importing the subsequent FIFO/command-processor rewrite:

- b684c0d: unbound GX texture stages sample white instead of black;
- 2bbb122: correct GXSetChanCtrl diffuse-function encoding;
- 1dde08f: apply depth correction to the projection matrix;
- 1a15801: bound RGBA8 conversion writes for partial edge tiles.

These were evaluated as a narrow compatibility set because each directly concerns a
symptom visible in the supplied frame: black materials, lighting-dependent
actors, depth/distance behavior, and malformed texture edges. The combined
physical build failed its first file-slot-2 stability run during Morph Ball.
All four changes were therefore removed from the hardware build. Retain this
file only as a record for a future one-change-at-a-time isolated bisect.

Do not describe this as an Aurora rebase. Current Aurora main contains a large
GX FIFO, command-processor, shader, texture, and recording refactor that has not
been imported or validated here.

The same correction pass removes two rejected local mitigations:

- the first tutorial door is no longer hidden after its open state; the
  original model/animation path is restored because abrupt disappearance is
  not a valid door animation fix;
- the 10 ms frontend audio transition ramp is removed because physical
  listening rejected it and the device log instead shows Amuse source bursts
  above full scale and hundreds of discontinuities with a healthy output queue.

Fog diagnostics are summarized every five seconds instead of logging normal
per-material fog on/off changes tens of thousands of times.
